Chapter: TcoDirectArgReads

 The loop multiplies by ten each turn and adds one to the parameter it
 accumulates into, so the fault is a wrong number rather than a hang:
 correct is 101, and reading the clobbered parameter gives 1001. There
 is no diagnostic and no fault, which is what makes this shape worse
 than the tco-shuffle-spill one it sits beside.

Section: Fixture

  Box = record {
   v : Integer
  }

  mk : Integer -> Box
  mk (x) = Box { v = x }

  loop4 : Integer, Box, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop4 (i) (s) (acc) (n) =
   if i >= n then acc
   else let s2 = mk (s.v * 10)
   in loop4 (i + 1) s2 (s.v + 1) n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("acc=" & show (loop4 0 (Box { v = 1 }) 0 3))
  end
